    categories: ["geopolitica"],
    title: "UK, France and China vote against UAE's Lana Nusseibeh at UN",
    summary: "UK, France and China vote against UAE's Lana Nusseibeh at UN Lana Nusseibeh's bid to become the next secretary-general of the United Nations suffered a setback on Friday after the UK , France and China all voted against the Emirati diplomat in the latest informal straw poll conducted to help determine who should replace Antonio Guterres. Along with the US and Russia , the countries make up three of the P5, the permanent members of the UN Security Council that can veto any prospective candidate for the world body's top job. While votes in the straw poll are cast anonymously, diplomatic and other sources close to the Security Council told Middle East Eye that the UK, China and France were the P5 members who had voted to \"discourage\" Nusseibeh's candidacy. The US, Russia and Israel - which is not currently part of the Security Council and thus does not vote - all back Nusseibeh, according to the same sources. In total, the UAE minister of state and former ambassador to the UN received seven \"encourage\" votes, six \"discourage\" votes and two \"no opinion\" votes - the same result she achieved in the last straw poll, held on 6 November. UN",
    preview: "UK, France and China vote against UAE's Lana Nusseibeh at UN Lana Nusseibeh's bid to become the next secretary-general of the United Nations suffered a setback on Friday after the UK , France and China all voted against the Emirati diplomat in the latest informal straw poll conducted to help determine who should replace Antonio Guterres. Along with the US and Russia , the countries make up three of the P5, the permanent members of the UN Security Council that can veto any prospective candidate for the world body's top job.",
