    id: "e0bab2227ad7f2533692",
    cat: "geopolitica",
    categories: ["geopolitica"],
    title: "Rights group calls for ban on white phosphorus, cites Israel's use in Gaza",
    summary: "Rights group calls for ban on white phosphorus, cites Israel's use in Gaza Cairo-based rights group, Maat for Peace, Development and Human Rights, has called for an explicit ban on the use of white phosphours, which has repeatedly been used by Israel in Gaza and southern Lebanon, Al Jazeera reported. White phosphorus can cause severe burns, ignite repeatedly and produce intense heat and toxic smoke. Human rights groups and The New York Times said in June they have documented Israel's use of the chemical white phosphorus over civilian areas in Lebanon. White phosphorus is not banned under international law, but it is illegal to use the chemical in and near populated areas since it can cause widespread harm. Israel has been accused by the international human rights community for decades of using the substance in a way that puts civilians in danger. In a working paper submitted at the review session for the UN Convention on Certain Conventional Weapons, the group said the current treaty has glaring gaps that allow for the use of white phosphorus. Following an impasse after talks started on Monday, the conference ran over time and ended early on Saturday, with states agreeing to continue talks aimed at developing measures on lethal autonomous weapons by 2028.",
    preview: "Rights group calls for ban on white phosphorus, cites Israel's use in Gaza Cairo-based rights group, Maat for Peace, Development and Human Rights, has called for an explicit ban on the use of white phosphours, which has repeatedly been used by Israel in Gaza and southern Lebanon, Al Jazeera reported. White phosphorus can cause severe burns, ignite repeatedly and produce intense heat and toxic smoke. Human rights groups and The New York Times said in June they have documented Israel's use of the chemical white phosphorus over civilian areas in Lebanon.",
    body: "Rights group calls for ban on white phosphorus, cites Israel's use in Gaza Cairo-based rights group, Maat for Peace, Development and Human Rights, has called for an explicit ban on the use of white phosphours, which has repeatedly been used by Israel in Gaza and southern Lebanon, Al Jazeera reported. White phosphorus can cause severe burns, ignite repeatedly and produce intense heat and toxic smoke.\n\nHuman rights groups and The New York Times said in June they have documented Israel's use of the chemical white phosphorus over civilian areas in Lebanon. White phosphorus is not banned under international law, but it is illegal to use the chemical in and near populated areas since it can cause widespread harm. Israel has been accused by the international human rights community for decades of using the substance in a way that puts civilians in danger.\n\nIn a working paper submitted at the review session for the UN Convention on Certain Conventional Weapons, the group said the current treaty has glaring gaps that allow for the use of white phosphorus. Following an impasse after talks started on Monday, the conference ran over time and ended early on Saturday, with states agreeing to continue talks aimed at developing measures on lethal autonomous weapons by 2028.",
