    title: "Pro-Palestine donor James Chambers released, says 'my sacrifice is very small'",
    summary: "Pro-Palestine donor James Chambers released, says 'my sacrifice is very small' Spain's High Court has released pro-Palestinian donor and US media heir James Cox Chambers Jr. on conditional bail, while it considers an extradition request by the United States, according to a court ruling released on Friday (November 20). The court said it had decided to release Chambers after US authorities acknowledged what they described as substantial and unintentional errors in the Spanish translation of an FBI agent's sworn statement submitted in support of the extradition request. On his release, Chambers told Reuters he believed the accusations against him were baseless and politically motivated, adding that he had been alone in a cell for what \"felt like a long time\". \"I'm glad that this is a step in the right direction,\" he said. Chambers added: \"In the end of the day, I understand that most of the sacrifice I've had to make is very, very small in relation, to the struggle that that we are all a part of for the Palestinian people, for their liberation, for their sovereignty, for their respect, for the right to live.\" \"But in the context of just being alone in a cell all the time, it feels like a long time. I just missed my family. I really missed my family and my friends,” Chambers said. Chambers, whose family owns Cox Enterprises, was arrested at the request of US authorities on July 10 while on holiday in Ibiza. He has been held in custody since on accusations including riot, conspiracy to commit riot and international money laundering. Chambers, known as Fergie, denies wrongdoing. Separately, Chambers' lawyers said they were challenging a raid by Irish police on his family home in Dublin, which they said was conducted at the request of US authorities and involved the seizure of electronic devices and other property. His legal team said it would seek judicial review unless authorities clarify the legal basis for the operation. Report by Reuters Chambers said his sacrifice was very small in relation to the struggle for the Palestinian people. (Reuters)",
    preview: "Pro-Palestine donor James Chambers released, says 'my sacrifice is very small' Spain's High Court has released pro-Palestinian donor and US media heir James Cox Chambers Jr. on conditional bail, while it considers an extradition request by the United States, according to a court ruling released on Friday (November 20). The court said it had decided to release Chambers after US authorities acknowledged what they described as substantial and unintentional errors in the Spanish translation of an FBI agent's sworn statement submitted in support of the…",
    body: "Pro-Palestine donor James Chambers released, says 'my sacrifice is very small' Spain's High Court has released pro-Palestinian donor and US media heir James Cox Chambers Jr. on conditional bail, while it considers an extradition request by the United States, according to a court ruling released on Friday (November 20). The court said it had decided to release Chambers after US authorities acknowledged what they described as substantial and unintentional errors in the Spanish translation of an FBI agent's sworn statement submitted in support of the extradition request.\n\nOn his release, Chambers told Reuters he believed the accusations against him were baseless and politically motivated, adding that he had been alone in a cell for what \"felt like a long time\". \"I'm glad that this is a step in the right direction,\" he said. Chambers added: \"In the end of the day, I understand that most of the sacrifice I've had to make is very, very small in relation, to the struggle that that we are all a part of for the Palestinian people, for their liberation, for their sovereignty, for their respect, for the right to live.\" \"But in the context of just being alone in a cell all the time, it feels like a long time.\n\nI just missed my family. I really missed my family and my friends,” Chambers said. Chambers, whose family owns Cox Enterprises, was arrested at the request of US authorities on July 10 while on holiday in Ibiza. He has been held in custody since on accusations including riot, conspiracy to commit riot and international money laundering. Chambers, known as Fergie, denies wrongdoing. Separately, Chambers' lawyers said they were challenging a raid by Irish police on his family home in Dublin, which they said was conducted at the request of US authorities and involved the seizure of electronic devices and other property.\n\nHis legal team said it would seek judicial review unless authorities clarify the legal basis for the operation. Report by Reuters Chambers said his sacrifice was very small in relation to the struggle for the Palestinian people. (Reuters)",
